  "_what": "PIM 100.93 -- Microsoft's default PIM policy settings. THIS TABLE is what 'Microsoft default' means in PIM Manager: the same in every tenant, always available. Microsoft's documentation does not state these defaults, so each value is CAPTURED from a policy nobody ever changed in a fresh tenant. Per policy type: 'fields' = setting id -> { value, source, capturedDate, verified }; 'exceptions' = object id (an Entra role's role definition / template id) -> { setting id: value } for objects whose default differs from the type's. The job policy-defaults reads this tenant's untouched policies as a CROSS-CHECK only: a difference is reported, it never changes what is written. A change of a value here in a later release is an ADVISORY for that setting (a choice made earlier is asked again).",
  "_status": "directoryRole: measured 2026-10-12 on a fresh tenant (145 Entra role policies, all never modified) incl. the 19 roles whose activation asks for multifactor authentication -- verified. groupMember / groupOwner: measured 2026-10-12 on 8 never-modified PIM for Groups policies (4 groups, member + owner, one identical rule set) -- verified; activation asks for a reason only, NOT for multifactor authentication. azureRole: NOT measured yet -- verified = false, so it can neither be chosen nor written.",
